# HomeAV Privacy Policy

_Last updated: [DATE]_

HomeAV is a client app for media servers that you run yourself. This policy explains what the app does with data.

## Data we collect
**None.** HomeAV has no developer-operated servers, accounts, analytics, advertising or tracking. We do not receive your data.

## Data stored on your device
- **Sign-in token**: stored in the system Keychain, removed when you sign out.
- **Preferences, favourites, watch progress and cached artwork**: stored locally on your device.
- **Server address and username**: stored locally so you don't have to re-enter them.

## Where the app connects
- **Your own server**, at the address you enter. Your credentials and requests go only to that server. Its operator, which may be you, controls what it logs and keeps.
- **TMDB image service** (`image.tmdb.org`), to show posters for requests. Like any image host, it can see your device's IP address.
- **Your local network**, if you open Network & Diagnostics, to list devices advertising on it. Nothing from this is sent anywhere.

## Sharing
We do not sell, share or transfer your data to third parties.

## Children
HomeAV does not collect personal information from anyone, including children.

## Changes
Updates to this policy will be posted on this page with a new date.

